            "question": "How much does a stamped concrete patio cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Stamped work costs more than a plain broom finish because of the color, stamping and sealing labour. Size, pattern and site prep all affect the price — use our estimator for a ballpark, then we confirm with a free on-site visit in Orem, Provo, Pleasant Grove and nearby.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What stamp patterns and colors can I choose?",
            "answer": "<p>Ashlar slate, cobblestone, brick, wood-plank and more, in a wide range of integral colors, stains and release tones. We'll walk you through samples during the design step so it matches your home.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does stamped concrete hold up in Utah?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — when it's based, reinforced, sloped and sealed correctly. We seal every decorative pour and recommend resealing every few years to keep the color rich and protect against freeze-thaw and UV fade.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is stamped concrete cheaper than pavers or natural stone?",
            "answer": "<p>Usually, yes. You get the look of premium stone or brick as one continuous, low-maintenance surface with no shifting joints and no weeds — generally at a lower installed cost.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
